From: Metalio BSP maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: physmap: preserve the size of unbanked resources

The Wi-Fi layout maps a 6 MiB read-only cramfs resource. Rounding its map
size down to a power of two advertises only 4 MiB to MTD, so mtd_point()
rejects a complete image larger than 4 MiB. Only GPIO-banked mappings need
the window-order calculation; use the exact resource size otherwise.

--- a/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
@@ -519,9 +519,9 @@
 			info->maps[i].phys = res->start;
 
 		info->win_order = fls64(resource_size(res)) - 1;
-		info->maps[i].size = BIT(info->win_order +
-					 (info->gpios ?
-					  info->gpios->ndescs : 0));
+		info->maps[i].size = info->gpios ?
+			BIT(info->win_order + info->gpios->ndescs) :
+			resource_size(res);
 
 		info->maps[i].map_priv_1 = (unsigned long)dev;
 
